Async alembic environment generated by advanced-alchemy (asyncio template).

Local modifications are confined to the marked "Local additions" block in
env.py (model imports + geoalchemy2 autogenerate helpers). Keep everything
else identical to the installed template:
.venv/.../advanced_alchemy/alembic/templates/asyncio/

Day-to-day commands (need LITESTAR_APP=geometrikks.server.core:create_app):

    uv run litestar database make-migrations -m "describe change"
    uv run litestar database upgrade
    uv run litestar database show-current-revision

At app startup, geometrikks.server.migrations.migrate_database() runs
`alembic upgrade head` automatically (in a worker thread). drop_on_startup
(DB_DROP_ON_STARTUP=true) wipes and re-migrates, but only when
APP_ENVIRONMENT=development; it is refused with an error log elsewhere.

TimescaleDB objects (hypertables, continuous aggregates, policies) are
deliberately NOT managed by alembic — server/timescale.py applies them
idempotently after migrations at startup. Never add timescale DDL to a
revision. The PostGIS extension is created in the initial revision.
